      ":question/problem": "![](images/f7/f757ffa45b20e043ad461cb0dfa9c486cf73466b1d8d87fa0ffad00bc01af960.png)\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is defined and differentiable on $[- 1, 5]$. The graph of $f^{\u2032}(x)$, the derivative of $f(x)$, is shown above, where the areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $4$ and $1$, respectively (from left to right). Find the maximum value of $f(x)$ on the interval $[- 1, 5]$ given that $f(5) =-8$."
